  "_meta": {
    "owner": "docs/architecture/class-system-ideal.md 7b.4",
    "status": "DIAGNOSTIC, NOT A BALANCE PROPOSAL. Deliberately not named aptitudes.v2 - it is not a successor version and must never be published as one.",
    "note": "Reciprocal-consumed contests (reduction, amplification, penetration) resized so a FULL allocation delivers a total effect comparable to a full allocation of a sigmoid-consumed contest (x1.9, not x4 / x11). Tests whether defensive dominance under free build is a coefficient-sizing error or a structural one. Result: best marginal +3.56% -> +1.67%, dead aptitudes 5 -> 4. Most of the cause, not all of it (ideal 8.7)."
  },
  "grant": {
    "_note": "FREE BUILD (owner, 2026-08-25): the player has no class, so there is no class price and no posture surcharge - every point costs one point. The withdrawn price block is class-system-ideal.md 7a.3; what it was FOR now lives entirely in read.*.shareExponentMilli.",
    "aptitudePointsPerTheta": 3,
    "skillPointsPerTheta": 1
  },
  "read": {
    "_note": "PS-3, made into two tunable FUNCTIONS rather than two hard-coded reads. Both take the aptitude share of the spent points; neither takes an absolute count. Share is bounded [0,1], which is what makes level cancel at parity (ssot-power-scale.md 2) - an absolute read grows the gap between two builds proportional to Theta and saturates every sigmoid by Theta=300 (measured: class-rps-balance-2026-08-25.md 3.1).",
    "contest": {
      "_note": "value = kMilli/1000 * share^gamma * spanPoints. spanPoints is how many CONTEST POINTS one whole allocation is worth - a different concept from stats.accuracyScale, which is how many contest points move a probability. Both must exist; neither may be derived from the other.",
      "spanPoints": 100.0,
      "shareExponentMilli": 1000
    },
    "magnitude": {
      "_note": "value = kMilli/1000 * share^gamma * P(Theta). The ladder supplies the scale; the player supplies the share.",
      "shareExponentMilli": 1000
    }
  },
  "familyRead": {
    "_note": "THE unitClass DECISION, as one reviewable block rather than 48 per-edge flags - because the read mode is a property of the CHANNEL (what the formula compares it against), never of the edge that feeds it. Rule (measured, class-rps-balance-2026-08-25.md 3.1): a family compared against baseLong - the hit itself - is a magnitude; a family feeding a bounded ratio through a small scale is a contest.",
